Note: SharpBastion invokes Claude CLI non-interactively (`--print`, JSON
output, no TTY) as a subprocess. This is a programmatic/automated usage
pattern — confirm it is permitted under Anthropic's terms of service for
your account and use case before enabling the Claude CLI fallback.

Note: SharpBastion's Kagi integration (Client/KagiClient.cs) calls the Kagi
Search API directly via HttpClient (POST https://kagi.com/api/v0/search),
authenticating with an API key supplied through the 'KAGI_API_KEY'
environment variable. Search queries are only ever those the model itself
proposes via a <kagi_search> tag, gated by IKagiSearchProtocol — see
README.md's Architecture > Protocols section. Confirm your Kagi account's
terms permit this usage pattern before overriding the protocol for unattended
execution.